WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.079
But?

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.748
- But there will be a price.
- Name it.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.670
- Who was she?
- My sister.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

5
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.277
Corporations like Umbrella.

6
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.710
think they're above the law.

7
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.878
But they're not.

8
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.951
There are hundreds of thousands of us
who think the same all over the world.

9
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.675
Some of us provide information.

10
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.517
Others give their support.

11
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.990
Some take more direct action.

12
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.359
Like you.

13
00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.751
If your friends had been more thorough.
they would've seen through my false lD.

14
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.356
Then all the red flags
would've gone off.

15
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.348
Quantico. NSA. ViCAP. all the rest.

16
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.956
There's no way I could've
infiltrated the Hive.

17
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.677
So you sent your sister.

18
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.595
We needed something concrete.
anything to expose Umbrella to the press.

19
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.553
Proof of the research
going on down here.

20
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.152
What kind of research?

21
00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.510
The illegal kind.

22
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.794
Genetic.

23
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.472
Viral.

24
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.152
My sister was going to smuggle out a
sample of the virus they were developing.

25
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.915
How was she going to make it out?

26
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.072
She had a contact within the Hive.
someone I never met.

27
00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.792
They had access to security codes.
surveillance. everything she needed.

28
00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.477
So why didn't she make it?

29
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.596
Maybe she trusted the wrong person.

30
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.432
Maybe they set her up.

31
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.031
Kept the virus for themselves.

32
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.278
Do you have any idea what the T-virus
would be worth on the open market?

33
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.231
- Worth all this?
- Yeah.

34
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.793
To someone.

35
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.869
- Don't shoot!
- Close that door!

36
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.116
- They're behind us!
- Close the door!

37
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.754
Get off!

38
00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.633
Son of a bitch!

39
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.114
- You OK?
- Yeah.

40
00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.473
Right behind us.
What about this door?

41
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.438
They're waiting there too.

42
00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.914
And that way?

43
00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.112
Dead end. There's no way
out of the Queen's chamber.

44
00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.638
So we wait.
Someone doesn't hear from you.

45
00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.559
they'll send backup or something.
Right?

46
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.708
What? What's wrong?

47
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.114
- We don't have much time.
- Those blast doors we passed

48
00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.836
on the way in from the mansion.
they seal shut in under an hour.

49
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.993
If we're not out by then.
we're not getting out.

50
00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.319
What are you talking about?
They can't just bury us alive down here.

51
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.434
Containing the incident is
the only fail-safe plan they had...

52
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.835
against possible contamination.

53
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.678
And you're telling us this now.
when we're trapped

54
00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:48.032
- half a mile underground?
- We have to find a way out of this room.

55
00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.798
What are you doing?

56
00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.799
- Where are you going?
- I'm turning her back on.

57
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.309
- That's not a good idea.
- She'll know a way out.

58
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.110
That homicidal bitch killed my team.

59
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.039
That homicidal bitch may be
our only way out of here.

60
00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.994
Considering the way she's been treated.
she'll be real happy to help us out.

61
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.237
That circuit breaker you were
talking about. Can you bypass it?

62
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.198
- Yeah.
- So do it.

63
00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.192
Circuit breaker's disabled.

64
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.957
This time. if I hit the switch.
she won't shut down. She'll fry.

65
00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.557
The charge must've damaged her boards.

66
00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.716
There you are.

67
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.833
Things. I gather.
have gone out of control.

68
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.998
Give me that switch right now.
I'll fry your ass!

69
00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.637
I did warn you. didn't I?

70
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.959
- T ell us what's going on down here.
- Research and development.

71
00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.593
What about the T-virus?

72
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.473
The T-virus was a major
medical breakthrough.

73
00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.676
Although it clearly also possessed

74
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.878
highly profitable military applications.

75
00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.991
How does it explain those things?

76
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.397
Even in death. the human body
remains active.

77
00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.474
Hair and fingernails continue to grow.
New cells are produced.

78
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.749
And the brain holds a small electrical
charge that takes months to dissipate.

79
00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.793
The T-virus provides a massive jolt.
both to cellular growth

80
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.878
and to those trace electrical impulses.

81
00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.629
Put quite simply. it reanimates the body.

82
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.196
It brings the dead back to life?

83
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.752
Not fully. The subjects have
the simplest of motor functions.

84
00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.953
Perhaps a little memory.
Virtually no intelligence.

85
00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.876
They are driven by the basest
of impulses. the most basic of needs.

86
00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.829
- Which is?
- The need to feed.

87
00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.396
- How do you kill them?
- Severing the top of the spinal column

88
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:04.871
or massive trauma to the brain
are the most effective methods.

89
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.597
You mean shoot them in the head.

90
00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.870
Why did you kill
everybody down here?

91
00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.470
The T-virus escaped
into the air conditioning system.

92
00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.196
And an uncontrolled pattern
of infection began.

93
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:22.315
The virus is protean. changing from
liquid to airborne to blood transmission

94
00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:27.196
depending on its environment.
It's almost impossible to kill.

95
00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.153
I couldn't allow it to escape
from the Hive.

96
00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.999
So. I took steps.

97
00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.270
- Steps?
- You must understand.

98
00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.519
Those who become infected.
I can't allow you to leave.

99
00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.995
- We're not infected.
- Just one bite.

100
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.237
one scratch from these creatures
is sufficient

101
00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.034
and then you become one of them.

102
00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:55.233
A check of my systems indicates
my main drive circuit breaker

103
00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:57.078
has been disabled.

104
00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.152
May I ask why?

105
00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.709
Insurance. We need a way out of here.

106
00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.354
If you refuse to help. we flip the switch.

107
00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.473
Understand?

108
00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.711
After you.

109
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.912
What the hell is this place?

110
00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:33.438
The utility tunnels. They run underneath
the Hive for water. gas and power lines.

111
00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.636
- Been in here before.
- Keep moving!

112
00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.593
- Going round in circles.
- The computer says...

113
00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.711
- Why listen to her?
- Enough!

114
00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:58.311
We have no choice but to keep moving
because those things are behind us.

115
00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.910
That mesh won't hold. Keep moving.

116
00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.870
- Hold it!
- There's so many of them!

117
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.159
Fuck!

118
00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.476
Up on the pipes. Up on the pipes!

119
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.796
Quickly. everyone. up on the pipes!

120
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.718
Come on. there's a way up!

121
00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.399
Keep them back!

122
00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.838
Go on up. move it!

123
00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.716
Get over here. There's too many of them!

124
00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.990
Go. go. go!

125
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:03.233
Go on!

126
00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.158
I can manage!

127
00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.713
- Rain.
- What?

128
00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.559
We have to do something
about your wounds.

129
00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.918
I'm fine.

130
00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.439
I said I'm fine.

131
00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.031
You like that. don't you?

132
00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.076
You like the way it tastes. don't you?

133
00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.236
Like the taste of that?

134
00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.872
She was right.

135
00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.351
We're all going to die down here.

136
00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.869
No. we're getting out.

137
00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.993
All of us.

138
00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.559
You OK?

139
00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.639
God!

140
00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:47.912
- Hold on!
- Come on!

141
00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.312
Help him.

142
00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.829
- I can't.
- What are you waiting for?

143
00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.678
I can't focus.

144
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.592
I can't see!

145
00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:18.912
- Go up!
- Get up there!

146
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.716
- Come on!
- Go!

147
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.798
- You can do it! Move!
- You got it!

148
00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.873
- Stay there.
- We'll get you.

149
00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:34.516
We need to cut this wire and throw it
to him. Then we'll get him.

150
00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.791
Hold on.

151
00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.957
That's lucky.

152
00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.998
I want you to go.

153
00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:55.188
- We're not leaving you.
- Yes. you are.

154
00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.716
You can't kill all of them.

155
00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.516
I'm not going anywhere.

156
00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.316
I want you to go. now!

157
00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:07.030
Please. just do it.

158
00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.078
Just do it now!

159
00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.551
Please!

160
00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.354
Go!

161
00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.315
You'll have to work for your meal!

162
00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.476
Come on.

163
00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:28.119
Give me your arm. OK?
Over my shoulder.

164
00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.396
Ready? Here we go.

165
00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.391
When I get out of here.

166
00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.955
I think I'll get laid.

167
00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.796
You might want to clean up first.

168
00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.316
Wait.

169
00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.315
Are you OK?

170
00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.229
Blue for the virus.
green for the antivirus.

171
00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:26.074
Blue for the virus.
green for the antivirus.

172
00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.189
- A cure.
- What are you talking about?

173
00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:32.231
There's a cure.

174
00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:35.797
The process can be reversed.

175
00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:39.231
There's a cure! You'll be OK.

176
00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.715
I was beginning to worry.

177
00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.155
This is where they kept the T-virus.

178
00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.275
How do you know all this?

179
00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.557
Because I was going to steal it.

180
00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.198
I was your sister's contact.

181
00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.312
- You betrayed her.
- I don't know.

182
00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.636
- You caused all this.
- I can't remember.

183
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.593
- The truth?
- I don't remember the truth.

184
00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.395
I don't understand this.

185
00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:57.757
It's gone. It's gone. It's not there.

186
00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.949
I can't.

187
00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:04.037
I just can't. It's over.

188
00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:16.150
I can help you get the virus.
I have access to security codes.

189
00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.396
surweillance plans. the works.

190
00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.876
- But?
- But there's a price.

191
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.639
Name it.

192
00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:27.998
You have to guarantee me that
you'll bring this Corporation down.

193
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.751
Thank you!

194
00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:46.515
We can still make it out of here.
Come with me.

195
00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:51.557
We can have everything
we've ever wanted.

196
00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:56.551
The money's out there waiting.
You wouldn't believe how much.

197
00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.550
Is that how you thought
all my dreams would come true?

198
00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.152
Please. I wouldn't want to shoot you.

199
00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.717
Might need the bullets.

200
00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:11.751
Back off!

201
00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.837
I won't take any part in this.

202
00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:22.039
OK. but you can't just
wash your hands of this.

203
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.639
We work for the same company.
You knew what they did.

204
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.717
I was trying to stop them.

205
00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:35.399
You really believe that people like him
will ever change anything?

206
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:42.275
Nothing ever changes.

207
00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.028
Where...Where is...

208
00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.192
the antivirus?

209
00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:53.279
It's on the train.
where you found me.

210
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.711
You couldn't have been standing
more than three feet from it.

211
00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:02.752
I so nearly made it out.

212
00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:08.670
I didn't realise that bitch of a computer
had defence systems outside the Hive.

213
00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.318
In or out?

214
00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.995
In? Or out?

215
00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:18.910
I don't know what we had.

216
00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.917
But it's over.

217
00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:29.032
Back...

218
00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:31.992
the fuck off!

219
00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.315
I'm missing you already.

220
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.677
Your boyfriend's a real asshole.

221
00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:58.676
He shot the locking mechanism out.

222
00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:02.950
I can't believe that son of a bitch
is going to get away with this.

223
00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:04.559
I don't think so.

224
00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:10.233
I've been a bad. bad girl.

225
00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:10.275
Oh. my God.

226
00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.230
What the fuck is that?

227
00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.870
One of the Hive's early experiments.

228
00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:32.908
Produced by injecting the T-virus
directly into living tissue.

229
00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:35.395
The results were unstable.

230
00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:39.675
Now that it has fed on fresh DNA.
it will mutate...

231
00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:49.878
becoming a stronger. faster hunter.

232
00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.278
Great.

233
00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:55.438
If you knew it was loose.
why didn't you warn us?

234
00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.516
Because she was saving it.

235
00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:01.439
For us. Isn't that right?

236
00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:04.632
I didn't think any of you
would make it this far.

237
00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.359
Not without infection.

238
00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:09.632
Why didn't you tell us
about the antivirus?

239
00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:13.795
This long after infection.
there's no guarantee it would work.

240
00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:19.150
But there's a chance. Right?

241
00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:21.391
I don't deal in chance.

242
00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:31.515
Fuck it.

243
00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:46.030
- No pressure. guys.
- You require the four-digit access code.

244
00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:48.231
I can give you the code.

245
00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:52.149
- But first. you do something for me.
- What do you want?

246
00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:56.956
One of your group is infected.
I require her life for the code.

247
00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:00.476
The antivirus is right there
on the platform!

248
00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:04.236
I'm sorry. but it's a risk I cannot take.

249
00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:10.274
She's right. It's the only way.

250
00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:12.471
You'll have to kill me.

251
00:25:15.960 --> 00:25:18.235
Otherwise. we all die down here.

252
00:25:25.360 --> 00:25:28.591
The glass is reinforced.
but it won't hold forever.

253
00:25:33.120 --> 00:25:34.599
Do it.

254
00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:36.518
- Get up.
- Just do it.

255
00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:38.199
- Please.
- Do it!

256
00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:39.833
You don't have long to decide.

257
00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:43.350
- You have no choice.
- Kill her now!

258
00:25:43.560 --> 00:25:45.596
- Get up!
- You don't have any choice.

259
00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:47.752
- Just do it now!
- I can't!

260
00:25:47.960 --> 00:25:49.996
- Kill her now. Do it.
- Please.

261
00:25:50.320 --> 00:25:53.118
- Kill her. Kill her now!
- Just do it.

262
00:25:56.160 --> 00:25:57.912
Kill her!

263
00:26:26.120 --> 00:26:30.033
The bitch wouldn't open the door.
so I had to fry her.

264
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:33.357
Move!

265
00:26:40.920 --> 00:26:44.595
- What the fuck was that?
- It's a long story.

266
00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.311
Start it up.

267
00:27:05.520 --> 00:27:07.431
I'll get the virus.

268
00:27:41.720 --> 00:27:44.359
I'm missing you already.

269
00:27:48.840 --> 00:27:51.149
OK. we're in business.

270
00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.468
Full power! We're leaving!

271
00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:13.230
I don't want to be one of those things.

272
00:28:16.600 --> 00:28:18.989
Walking around without a soul.

273
00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:22.916
You won't.

274
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:26.157
When the time comes...

275
00:28:26.360 --> 00:28:28.237
you'll take care of it.

276
00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:32.549
No one else is going to die.

277
00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:45.950
Here.

278
00:29:46.280 --> 00:29:49.033
I'm not dead yet.

279
00:29:49.240 --> 00:29:50.992
I think I'll have that back.

280
00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.516
I could kiss you. you bitch.

281
00:30:00.840 --> 00:30:03.957
What the hell's going on back there?

282
00:30:14.400 --> 00:30:18.029
- Get us the fuck out of here.
- Any faster. we'll come off the rails.

283
00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:34.028
Open the doors!

284
00:31:55.440 --> 00:31:58.318
Open the doors! Now!

285
00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:41.270
I failed all of them.

286
00:33:44.200 --> 00:33:45.872
I failed.

287
00:33:47.200 --> 00:33:50.431
Listen to me.
There is nothing else you could've done.

288
00:33:51.240 --> 00:33:53.470
The Corporation's guilty here. not you.

289
00:33:53.680 --> 00:33:55.796
And we finally have the proof.

290
00:33:56.320 --> 00:34:00.472
And that way. Umbrella
can't get...away with this.

291
00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:04.115
I mean. we can finally...

292
00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:06.436
What is it?

293
00:34:08.120 --> 00:34:11.749
You're infected. but you'll be OK.
I'm not losing you.

294
00:34:20.080 --> 00:34:23.038
- Help!
- Help him! What are you doing?

295
00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:39.429
He's mutating.

296
00:34:40.280 --> 00:34:42.669
I want him in the Nemesis Program.

297
00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:50.876
What's happening?

298
00:35:14.680 --> 00:35:16.955
I want her quarantined.
Close observation

299
00:35:17.160 --> 00:35:18.957
and a full series of blood tests.

300
00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:22.752
Let's see if she's infected.

301
00:35:23.520 --> 00:35:25.636
Take her to the Raccoon City facility.

302
00:35:26.800 --> 00:35:29.951
Then assemble the team.
We're reopening the Hive.

303
00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:33.157
I want to know what went on down there.

304
00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:36.354
Just do it.

305
00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:47.516
Who's in there?

306
00:36:49.320 --> 00:36:51.436
Let me out!

307
00:36:51.640 --> 00:36:54.200
Let me out!

308
00:36:54.400 --> 00:36:55.799
Let me out!

309
00:36:56.305 --> 00:37:56.292
